### 🥈 Second Largest Element in an Array

The goal is to find the second largest element in an array without sorting it.

* Initialize two variables to keep track of the **largest** and **second largest** elements.
* Traverse through the array and compare each element with the largest element.
* If the current element is greater than the largest, update both largest and second largest.
* Otherwise, if the current element is smaller than the largest but greater than the second largest, update the second largest.
* After traversing the entire array, the second largest variable contains the required answer.

**Time Complexity:** `O(n)`
**Space Complexity:** `O(1)`

### Solution

class Solution {
    public int secondLargestElement(int[] nums) {
       int largest =Integer.MIN_VALUE;
       int slargest=Integer.MIN_VALUE;
       for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++)
       {
        if(nums[i]>largest)
        {
            slargest=largest;
            largest=nums[i];
        }
        else if(nums[i]<largest && nums[i]>slargest) slargest=nums[i];
       }
       return slargest==Integer.MIN_VALUE?-1:slargest;
    }
}
